cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Quantum CNN vs Classical CNN for Medical Image Segmentation"
abstract: "Systematic benchmarking of 13 segmentation models — classical CNNs, quaternion CNNs, quantum QCNNs (PennyLane and Qiskit), and a hybrid quantum–classical architecture — on two brain-MRI segmentation tasks: brainstem (3 structures) and HAMMERS (8 parietal-lobe regions). Every model is trained in both 2D axial-slice and full 3D volumetric mode with per-subject Dice evaluation and statistical testing (Friedman omnibus + bootstrap-paired comparisons)."
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-19
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/robbinc91/qcnn-vs-cnn-medical-imaging"
